---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { contactEmail, updated, legalName } from "../legal";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

const h2 = "prose-h2";
const p = "prose-p";
const ul = "prose-ul";
const link = "prose-a";
---

<Layout
  title="Support — Minnie"
  description="How to reach a real person about Minnie: billing, bugs, licence keys, and account deletion. One email address, answered by the person who built her."
>
  <Navbar />

  <main class="legal">
    <a href={base} class="legal__back mono">← back to home</a>

    <h1 class="legal__h1">Support</h1>
    <p class="legal__date mono">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p class={p} style="margin-top:28px;">
      Minnie is made by one person, and that same person answers the email. There is
      no ticket queue and no bot in front of it.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Email</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      <a class={link} href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a> — for
      anything at all: billing, bugs, licence keys, refunds, feature requests, or
      deleting your account. Expect a reply within <strong>two working days</strong>,
      usually sooner.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>What to include</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      None of this is required, but each one saves a round trip:
    </p>
    <ul class={ul}>
      <li><strong>Billing or licence</strong> — the email address you paid with.</li>
      <li><strong>A bug</strong> — your macOS version, Minnie's version (Settings ▸ About), and what you were doing when it happened.</li>
      <li><strong>She stopped responding</strong> — whether the pet still appears and whether she speaks, which tells us instantly whether it is the agent or the app.</li>
      <li><strong>Anything visual</strong> — a screenshot beats a paragraph.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class={h2}>Common ones</h2>
    <ul class={ul}>
      <li><strong>You bought Minnie before making an account.</strong> Your key still works — open <strong>Settings ▸ Account ▸ "Have a licence key?"</strong> and paste the key from your purchase email.</li>
      <li><strong>Moving to a new Mac.</strong> A licence runs on three at once. If you have retired one, email us and we will free the slot.</li>
      <li><strong>macOS says the app cannot be checked for malware.</strong> Beta builds are not yet notarised by Apple; the <a class={link} href={`${base}download`}>download page</a> explains how to open it anyway.</li>
      <li><strong>Refunds and cancellation</strong> — see the <a class={link} href={`${base}refund`}>Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</a>. Thirty days, no reason needed.</li>
      <li><strong>Deleting your account and data</strong> — ask, and we do it. What lives on your Mac you can delete yourself; the <a class={link} href={`${base}privacy`}>Privacy Policy</a> says where it is.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class={h2}>Reporting something security-related</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Minnie runs an AI agent with real access to your Mac, so we take this seriously.
      Email the same address with "security" in the subject and we will reply first.
      Please give us a chance to fix it before publishing.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Who you are dealing with</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Minnie is operated by {legalName}. Our <a class={link} href={`${base}terms`}>Terms of Service</a>, <a class={link} href={`${base}privacy`}>Privacy Policy</a> and <a class={link} href={`${base}refund`}>Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</a> apply to
      everything here.
    </p>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
